# Local-only defaults for the Settings screen's two connection fields, and
# (optionally) the GoldAPI.io / Alpha Vantage keys used on the Gold and Stocks
# Manage screens.
#
# To use: copy this file to `config/.env` (same folder, drop the `.example`) and fill
# in your values. The app reads it at startup and prefills the fields; it never
# connects or fetches a price on its own, and a value you have already saved in the
# browser (Settings, or the Gold/Stocks Manage screens' key inputs) always wins.
#
# `config/.env` is gitignored and must stay that way. The hosted site has no such
# file — there you type every value in by hand instead.
#
# The Client ID and Spreadsheet ID are not secrets. The OAuth Client ID is public by
# design: it is visible in the browser either way. The Spreadsheet ID names a document
# without granting access to it — reading the Sheet still requires signing in as
# someone it is shared with. GOLDAPI-KEY and ALPHAVANTAGE-KEY *are* real credentials —
# treat them like any other API key. All four are kept out of git because this file is
# gitignored; only this placeholder-filled `.example` copy is tracked.
#
# No financial data belongs in this file. Only the keys below are read; anything else
# here is ignored. (Currency rates need no key at all — open.er-api.com is a free,
# no-signup endpoint — so there's nothing to add here for that one.)

# Google Cloud Console -> Credentials -> your OAuth 2.0 Client ID (type: Web application)
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com

# From your Sheet's URL: docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<THIS PART>/edit
SPREADSHEET_ID=

# Free key from https://www.goldapi.io/ — prefills the Gold Manage screen's
# "Fetch latest 24k price" key input. Optional; leave blank to keep typing it in.
GOLDAPI-KEY=

# Free key from https://www.alphavantage.co/support/#api-key — prefills the Stocks
# Manage screen's "Fetch latest close" key input. Optional; leave blank to keep
# typing it in.
ALPHAVANTAGE-KEY=